        "text_nYUUwP": {
          "type": "text",
          "name": "t:names.text",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<p>Not sure where to start? Post oak and hickory cover most beef, fruit wood like apple wood and cherry wood keeps poultry and pork shoulder mild and sweet, and a blend lets you dial in the flavor profile you want. Mesquite is the boldest of the group, so most pit masters use it in smaller amounts or save it for steak and open-flame grilling.</p>",
