          },
          "blocks": {
            "accordion_row_rcarKK": {
              "type": "_accordion-row",
              "name": "t:names.accordion_row",
              "settings": {
                "heading": "What is the best wood for smoking meat?",
                "content": "",
                "open_by_default": true,
                "icon": "none",
                "width": 20
              },
              "blocks": {
                "text_jCmtdx": {
                  "type": "text",
                  "settings": {
                    "text": "<p>It depends on the protein and how much smoke<br/>you want. Post oak and hickory are reliable all-around choices for beef, mesquite delivers a bold<br/>flavor best used in moderation, and a milder wood like apple or cherry keeps poultry and pork<br/>mild and sweet. Many kitchens blend two types of wood to build a signature flavor profile.</p>",
                    "width": "100%",
                    "max_width": "none",
                    "alignment": "left",
                    "type_preset": "rte",
                    "font": "var(--font-body--family)",
                    "font_size": "1rem",
                    "weight": "",
                    "weight_active": "inherit",
                    "line_height": "normal",
                    "letter_spacing": "normal",
                    "case": "none",
                    "wrap": "pretty",
                    "color": "var(--color-foreground)",
                    "background": false,
                    "background_color": "#00000026",
                    "text_color": "#000000",
                    "active_color": "#d23d00",
                    "corner_radius": 0,
                    "padding-block-start": 0,
                    "padding-block-end": 0,
                    "padding-inline-start": 0,
                    "padding-inline-end": 0,
                    "padding-block-start-mobile": 0,
                    "padding-block-end-mobile": 0,
                    "padding-inline-start-mobile": 0,
                    "padding-inline-end-mobile": 0
                  },
                  "blocks": {}
                }
              },
              "block_order": [
                "text_jCmtdx"
              ]
            },
            "accordion_row_kWfkdt": {
              "type": "_accordion-row",
              "name": "t:names.accordion_row",
              "settings": {
                "heading": "Is your cooking wood ready to use?",
                "content": "",
                "open_by_default": false,
                "icon": "none",
                "width": 20
              },
              "blocks": {
                "text_niBtPk": {
                  "type": "text",
                  "settings": {
                    "text": "<p>Yes. Our wood is naturally aged in the Texas sun and<br/>heat-treated to a low, consistent moisture content, so it lights easily and produces clean, steady<br/>smoke straight off the pallet.</p>",
                    "width": "100%",
                    "max_width": "none",
                    "alignment": "left",
                    "type_preset": "rte",
                    "font": "var(--font-body--family)",
                    "font_size": "1rem",
                    "weight": "",
                    "weight_active": "inherit",
                    "line_height": "normal",
                    "letter_spacing": "normal",
                    "case": "none",
                    "wrap": "pretty",
                    "color": "var(--color-foreground)",
                    "background": false,
                    "background_color": "#00000026",
